loop\items\AI4DEV-57\gate2-kimi-sql.incomplete-run.txt:301: **K. proof-local (i)**: calls `sql`select public.complete_signup(...)`` as postgres superuser — fine. But note: `atomicityRaised !== ''` — if the function unexpectedly succeeded, leftBehind would show rows and check fails. Good.
loop\items\AI4DEV-57\gate2-kimi-sql.incomplete-run.txt:317: **S. One more SQL check**: `complete_signup` — `p_ip inet` parameter. The edge function passes `callerIp(request)` which is `string | null`. JSON null → SQL NULL. OK. String '203.0.113.7' → PostgREST casts to inet. Invalid string → error 400 (code 22P02?) → edge function maps to 409 (status >= 400 && < 500 → 409). A malformed-IP client gets a 409 with DB syntax error message. Covered in finding A.
loop\items\AI4DEV-57\gate2-kimi-sql.incomplete-run.txt:526: Let me also double check finding 2's reachability: does `complete_signup`'s insert of p_ip fail the whole transaction on bad inet? p_ip arrives as text through JSON → PostgREST casts to inet at function invocation, actually! The parameter is `inet`; PostgREST casts the JSON string to inet BEFORE the function body runs. An invalid inet string → error 22P02 at cast time → 400 → no writes at all. So the atomicity isn't even exercised; signup just fails. Still the availability/robustness point stands (garbage header → cannot complete signup, error message leaks raw cast error). And forged-but-valid IP stands regardless.
