loop\state\decisions.jsonl:96: {"id":"d87","date":"2026-07-23","title":"PM board = the 30 requirement items ONLY; bring-up and design batches live on the dev board","decision":"Founder ruling correcting the tree plan before the Linear push: the PM board (AI4GOOD-PM) holds exactly the 30 PRD requirement items in their wave projects - nothing else. The W0 bring-up items (test harness, at-config, CI, staging, the work skill + drills) and the 7 design batch items (Batch 0 system/shell + batches 1-6) are created on the DEV board (AI4GOOD-DEV) instead. Rationale: the PM tree mirrors the product, where a project's PM tree only ever carries scope requirements + the bootstrap item; bring-up and design batches are process work with no acceptance suites, no attribution bindings, and no pull ceremony, so on PM they would sit outside the status-authority model. On DEV they fit the existing mechanics: bring-up items close via the GitHub integration on merge; design batch items are managed with plain Linear calls and closed manually on the batch's real evidence (design gate green + founder gallery sign-off, recorded in git). Design commits cite AI4DEV item ids (the earlier AI4PM-nnn convention in design-session.md is amended). Supersedes the PM-project placement hypothesized in loop/decomp/README.md and TREE-REVIEW.md.","evidence":"Founder 2026-07-23 (UI items and bring-up should be on dev); README waves note, TREE-REVIEW push mechanics, design-session.md commit convention, and the tree-view artifact all updated in the same bundle.","status":"adopted"}
